  # 3 Indicators :

       - 1. (M15) Relative Strength Index (RSI).  Think of the RSI as a speedometer that measures how fast car prices are moving, and whether buyers or sellers are getting tired. It ranges from a score of 0 to 100, 
            It tells if the market is over-pumped (Overbought) or completely exhausted (Oversold).
              Sell Condition : When Price drops into Fibonacci 0.618 – 0.786  zone, the RSI on the M15 chart will often drop below 30 (meaning sellers are exhausted). should look for the moment the RSI line crosses back above 30 or 50. This proves that buyers are stepping back in.
              Buy Condition : When Price rises into Fibonacci 0.618 – 0.786  zone, look for the RSI to climb above 70 and then cross back below 70 or 50, proving sellers are taking control.
       - 2. (M15) Moving Average Convergence Divergence (MACD). Think of the MACD as a momentum camera. It doesn't look at individual price ticks; it looks at the overall shifting weight of the market,
            It consists of two lines and a bar chart (the histogram) that moves above and below a central "0" line.  It filters out "fake" price movements and tells you when the actual shift in power happens.
              Sell Condition : The easiest rule is the central 0 line. In A Sell Condition trade, wait for the MACD bars to switch from being above 0 (green/positive) to printing above 0 (red/negative).
              Buy Condition : The easiest rule is the central 0 line. In A Buy Condition trade, wait for the MACD bars to switch from being below 0 (red/negative) to printing above 0 (green/positive).
       - 3. (H1 Or M15) Exponential Moving Average (EMA50). Think of the EMA 50 as a moving floor or ceiling. It takes the average price of the last 50 candles but puts more weight on the most recent candles so it reacts quickly to sudden news or movements.
            It acts as a visual trend barrier. If the price is above it, the immediate trend is up. If the price is below it, the immediate trend is down.
              The Bounce Filter : Fibonacci  0.618 – 0.786  zone is a theoretical area where price might stop. The EMA 50 gives it a physical barrier.
              Sell Condition :  Wait for the price to hit Fibonacci 0.618 – 0.786 zone, struggle to go higher, and then close a candle completely below the M15 EMA 50 line. This acts as proof that the "ceiling" held.
              Buy Condition :  Wait for the price to hit Fibonacci 0.618 – 0.786 zone, struggle to go lower, and then close a candle completely above the M15 EMA 50 line. This acts as proof that the "floor" held.









